    // so they no longer try: the app derives every result from the events with the shared core replay
    // (src/core/scoring.ts computeState under the match's rules, which are frozen once the first rally exists,
    // see rosterFrozenOk) – result page, captain confirm, POTM, wallet, leaderboard, abandon and the
    // "finished" badge (firebaseBackend.matchFrom replaces the stored summary with the replay and flags a
    // disagreement for admin review: src/core/replay.ts). The rules enforce what makes that replay sound:
    //  - events change by one scorer step per write (eventsStepOk) with well-formed rallies and side A/B;
    //  - rules, firstServe, teams and set lineups already in use can't change once the first rally exists;
    //  - a scorer abandons only a match whose log never reached the shortest win and that was never won (1.4.5:
    //    scorerAbandonOk, maxEvents / wasWon); an admin who isn't part of the match resolves the rest (adminResolveOk);
